WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.000
On the Home screen, click Open project… and pick the project.

2
00:00:03.000 --> 00:00:06.000
Click Post.

3
00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:13.000
Post opens on one visible layer, S-H-O · Combine layers; the layer of the Stars workflow is added hidden. Nothing is offered to compute.

4
00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:16.000
Select the S-H-O · Combine layers layer.

5
00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:24.000
Read the picture as the software gives it: a grey veil over the nebula, flat colours, and crowded pink stars.

6
00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:27.000
Open the zoom list.

7
00:00:27.000 --> 00:00:30.000
Choose 100 %.

8
00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:38.000
At 100 %, the top-left corner: the stars are comet-shaped, the sky is a lifted grey, and the edge is black.

9
00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:41.000
Click Crop.

10
00:00:41.000 --> 00:00:44.000
Drag the top-left corner in until the comet stars and the black edge are outside the box.

11
00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:50.000
The box now holds 3655 × 2450 px.

12
00:00:50.000 --> 00:00:53.000
Click Apply.

13
00:00:53.000 --> 00:00:59.000
The picture is cropped and centred on the North America and the wall.

14
00:00:59.000 --> 00:01:02.000
Drag Sky to the left until the veil is gone and the sky is a dark grey: about −0,5.

15
00:01:02.000 --> 00:01:08.000
The sky is now a dark grey.

16
00:01:08.000 --> 00:01:11.000
Drag Contrast up until the wall and the dark lanes stand out: about +0,9.

17
00:01:11.000 --> 00:01:14.000
Drag Faint tones up until the outer filaments come up: about +0,5.

18
00:01:14.000 --> 00:01:20.000
The wall and the lanes have depth and the faint gas shows.

19
00:01:20.000 --> 00:01:23.000
Drag Saturation up until the palette has its colours: about +1,0.

20
00:01:23.000 --> 00:01:29.000
Gold and orange for H-alpha and S II, blue for O III.

21
00:01:29.000 --> 00:01:32.000
Drag Star color toward white: about −1,5.

22
00:01:32.000 --> 00:01:38.000
The stars lose their false pink.

23
00:01:38.000 --> 00:01:41.000
Drag Star size toward smaller: about −0,4.

24
00:01:41.000 --> 00:01:44.000
Drag Small stars toward less: about −0,3.

25
00:01:44.000 --> 00:01:50.000
Fewer and smaller small stars over the gas.

26
00:01:50.000 --> 00:01:53.000
Click the version name to rename it.

27
00:01:53.000 --> 00:01:58.000
The version is now called Default S-H-O.

28
00:01:58.000 --> 00:02:01.000
Click Export.

29
00:02:01.000 --> 00:02:04.000
Choose the JPEG format.

30
00:02:04.000 --> 00:02:09.000
Check the file, on the tutorial drive, then click Export.

31
00:02:09.000 --> 00:02:14.000
Save the project with Ctrl+S.
